FUN_0000_024f (VGA mode-set init helper): DGROUP near-pointer base loss + int/word pointer scaling.

Reached from the VGA mode-set FUN_0000_00e8 (line `FUN_0000_024f(0x726,param_3)`), just before its INT 10h
AX=13h.  param_1 = 0x726 is a DGROUP NEAR offset (the driver runs with DS=DGROUP=0x1c00); Ghidra dropped
the segment base and dereferenced the bare offset as a host address -> SIGSEGV.  asm 0x24f: `testw [bx];
je 0x246` (loop body 0x246: `movw [bx],0xa000; movw [bx+4],0x140`); `xchg ax,[0x724]` (WORD store DGROUP:
0x724=bx); `mov ax,[bx+4]`; call 02c1.  Also int-width scaling: param_1[2] scaled to byte +8 (should be
+4) and the 4-byte c724 store would clobber DGROUP:0x726.  Rebase to g_mem+DGROUP+off with 16-bit word
accesses.  Asm-verified base-0 MGAVIDEO offset 0x24f.
--- a/fist_mga.c
+++ b/fist_mga.c
@@ -997,14 +997,21 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_024f(int *param_1,undefined2 param_2)
 
 {
-  while (*param_1 == 0) {
-    *param_1 = -0x6000;
-    param_1[2] = 0x140;
+  /* PATCH 036: DGROUP near-pointer base loss + int/word scaling in the VGA mode-set init helper.
+   * asm 0x24f: entry `testw [bx]; je 0x246` where the loop body 0x246 does `movw [bx],0xa000;
+   * movw [bx+4],0x140`; then `xchg ax,[0x724]` (DGROUP:0x724 = bx, WORD), `mov ax,[bx+4]`, call 02c1.
+   * param_1 = bx = a DGROUP NEAR offset (0x726; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00); Ghidra dropped the segment base and
+   * dereferenced the bare 16-bit offset as a host pointer -> SIGSEGV, and typed the accesses as 4-byte
+   * `int` (param_1[2] scaled to +8, and the c724 store 4-byte -> would clobber DGROUP:0x726).  Rebase to
+   * g_mem+DGROUP+off with explicit 16-bit word accesses; word index 2 = byte +4. */
+  uint16_t off = (uint16_t)(uintptr_t)param_1;
+  uint16_t *p = (uint16_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + off);
+  while (p[0] == 0) {
+    p[0] = 0xa000;
+    p[2] = 0x140;
   }
-  LOCK();
-  UNLOCK();
-  _DAT_1000_c724 = param_1;
-  FUN_0000_02c1(param_1[2],param_2);
+  *(uint16_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c724) = off;
+  FUN_0000_02c1(p[2],param_2);
   return;
 }
 
